{"name":"Blue Lust","hex":"#012389","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"lust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of strong desire, especially such a feeling driven by sexual arousal.","A general want or longing, not necessarily sexual."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To look at or watch with a strong desire, especially of a sexual nature.","To desire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lust","blocks":[{"text":"Lust is an intense desire for something. Lust can take any form such as the lust for sexual activity, money, or power; but it can also take such mundane forms as the lust for food or the lust for redolence. Lust is similar to, but distinguished from, passion, in that properly ordered passion propels individuals to achieve benevolent goals whilst lust does not."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg/330px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lust","wikidata":"Q6498477"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg/500px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg/500px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail: Luxuria (Lust), in The Seven Deadly Sins and the Four Last Things, by Hieronymus Bosch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_(Luxuria).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Daemon.jpg/500px-Daemon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Daemon.jpg/500px-Daemon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A demon satiating his lust in a 13th-century manuscript","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaemon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg/500px-Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=